  "description": "Allocation-free XML serializer/deserializer built on C# incremental source generators. Serialization code is emitted at compile time, so there is no runtime reflection and no first-call warm-up. Measured against System.Xml.Serialization on the same documents (.NET 10): a typical payload deserializes 4.3x faster while allocating 5% of what the BCL allocates, and serializes 3.6x faster; a 100 MB document is 2.7x faster on 39% of the heap; a document nested 100 levels deep is 5.5x faster, because the parser is single-pass and depth does not multiply the work. The margin is smaller on .NET Framework, where span-based Parse and TryFormat are missing. Format-compatible with System.Xml.Serialization for the primitives, collections and xsi:type polymorphism it supports.",
  "id": "XmlSerDe",
